{"id":107298,"title":"Multiresolution Distance Volumes for Progressive Surface Compression","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=volume data compression rendering","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/m2/1/high_res_d/15013487.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"343979fd709bda7191a366cf17b10f5996371dd09ffc99ff773f0f58f99724aa","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793234413.2926793,"text_chars":36642,"abstract":"We present a surface compression method that stores surfaces as wavelet-compressed signed-distance volumes. Our approach enables the representation of surfaces with complex topology and arbitrary numbers of components within a single multiresolution data structure. This data structure elegantly handles topological modification at high compression rates. Our method does not require the costly and sometimes infeasible base mesh construction step required by subdivision surface approaches. We present several improvements over previous attempts at compressing signed-distance functions, including an 0(n) distance transform, a zero set initialization method for triangle meshes, and a specialized thresholding algorithm. We demonstrate the potential of sampled distance volumes for surface compression and progressive reconstruction for complex high genus surfaces.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/m2/1/high_res_d/15013487.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=volume data compression rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=volume data compression wavelet","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=multiresolution volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=lossy compression scientific volume data","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=hierarchical volume rendering wavelets multiresolution","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=wavelet volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=signed distance field mesh","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=signed box distance function","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=sphere signed distance function","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=wavelet based multiresolution rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=extended trilinear triangulation","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=multi-resolution volume visualization","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=octree volume compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=multiresolution decomposed volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=distance field compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=wavelet volume rendering compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=progressive encoding volumetric data","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=octree data structure compression","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1409942/?q=hierarchical wavelet compression"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1268-interpolated-discrete-values-gradients.md","name":"Interpolated Discrete Values & Gradients","k":6},{"path":"2285-wavelet-transform.md","name":"Wavelet Transform","k":5},{"path":"8260-3-d-spiht.md","name":"3-D SPIHT","k":2},{"path":"11840-multiresolution-distance-volumes-for-progressive-surface-com.md","name":"Multiresolution Distance Volumes for Progressive Surface Compression","k":1},{"path":"7647-wavelet-coefficient-trees.md","name":"Wavelet Coefficient Trees","k":2}]}